  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "For an array BBB of length MMM, we define f(B)f(B)f(B) as follows:\n\n\nInitialize score=0\\text{score} = 0score=0.\nThen, perform the following operation M−1M-1M−1 times:\n\nChoose an index iii (1≤i&lt;∣B∣1 \\leq i \\lt |B|1≤i&lt;∣B∣).\nAdd min⁡(Bi,Bi+1)\\min(B_i, B_{i+1})min(Bi​,Bi+1​) to score\\text{score}score, and then delete max⁡(Bi,Bi+1)\\max(B_i, B_{i+1})max(Bi​,Bi+1​) from BBB.\n\nThis reduces the length of BBB by exactly 111.\n\n\nf(B)f(B)f(B) is defined to be the maximum possible value of score\\text{score}score at the end of this process.\n\nYou are given an array AAA of length NNN.\n\nProcess QQQ updates on it.\n\nEach update gives you two integers iii and XXX. You must set Ai=XA_i = XAi​=X, and then compute the value of f(A)f(A)f(A).\n\nUpdates to the array are permanent.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and QQQ — the length of the array and the number of updates.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ – the initial elements of AAA.\nThe next QQQ lines describe the updates. Each of them contains two space-separated integers iii and XXX, meaning you should set Ai=XA_i = XAi​=X.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nAfter each update, output on a new line the value of f(A)f(A)f(A).",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N,Q≤2⋅1051 \\leq N, Q \\leq 2\\cdot 10^51≤N,Q≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Ai,X≤1091 \\leq A_i, X \\leq 10^91≤Ai​,X≤109",
      "1≤i≤N1 \\leq i \\leq N1≤i≤N",
      "The sum of NNN and the sum of QQQ over all test cases both won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
